+### Attention metadata
+
+Renderers classify outstanding tasks from structured state, never title text:
+
+- `metadata.attention="captain-input"` requests captain input and renders
+  orange `#FF9800`. This explicit request takes precedence over blockers.
+- `status="in_progress"` together with
+  `metadata.attention="agent-working"` and no `blockedBy` asserts that the agent
+  is actually working and renders green `#00E676`.
+- `metadata.attention="waiting"`, missing/unknown attention, pending status,
+  and blocked tasks render neutral gray `#B0B0B0`. A stale `in_progress` status
+  alone is never green.
+
+Todo list surfaces include a compact colored key with the plain-language labels
+`working`, `waiting`, and `needs you`, so attention is not communicated by color
+alone. Mutation-only tool responses stay compact and do not include the key.
+
+When a captain answers, clear `captain-input` by setting `attention` to
+`waiting`; only change it to `agent-working` in the same update that starts
+actual work. Before pausing, blocking, or handing control back, set `attention`
+to `waiting` (and move `in_progress` back to `pending` when appropriate).
+Supply `metadata.attentionReason` with an actionable reason, such as `awaiting
+CI`, `waiting for worker test results`, or `tests failed; fix assertion`.
+Clear obsolete reasons with `attentionReason: null` when resuming. A waiting
+state is not a failed state: only caller-supplied text reports a failure.
+
+There is no automatic worker-liveness binding, endpoint probe, or expiry timer.
+Callers own the truth of `agent-working`, including clearing stale assertions
+on interruption; a persisted explicit assertion is trusted on replay. The live
+widget animates only this asserted active state; historical tool/command
+snapshots stay static. See [overlay](overlay.md) and
+[reduced motion](configuration.md#reducedmotion).
+Completed/deleted tasks have no attention indicator. A legacy leading `● `
+title workaround is normalized away on create, subject update, or replay;
+the rest of the semantic title is preserved.
+
